{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: add a bounded resident-side MCP surface for querying actor work and inspecting exact durable items, so agents do not need to repeatedly download the full status projection and filter it with jq. The current MCP status digest is useful for orientation but capped; its adapter still fetches all of /v0/status before filtering. At durable depth about 1895, /v0/status was 3,613,729 bytes while /v0/status-summary was 31,685 bytes. Design a typed interface rather than accepting jq, JSONPath, or another free-form query language.","body":{"conditions":"Selection happens at the resident-service boundary before full projection JSON is encoded or transferred; the MCP adapter does not fetch /v0/status to answer the new query. The interface provides typed actor-work filters, stable bounded pagination or continuation, exact canonical event IDs, and explicit total/omitted counts. Open unclaimed requests addressed to the actor and stale commitments remain discoverable and are included by default unless the caller explicitly narrows them. Exact-ID inspection can return the statement or act, decision, commitment chain, provenance bases, and related artifacts needed for review and ratification without a full projection fetch. Existing status and wait behavior remains compatible. Tests use a large projection to prove bounded output and prove that the resident selective endpoint—not /v0/status—is used. Document the intended status-once, wait-for-deltas, selective-inspection workflow. If local Git ancestry is exposed, require an explicit target ref and label the result as nondurable local evidence.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}